{
  "dom_id": "step-q162567",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14184931/assets/9f2f77c6c2047dcd3f542fc0f640a68b45a4d40784d0e7eaacdcadb002c79de5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following shows the streamlines of this vector field?",
  "worked_solution": "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nOf the given options, the only level curves tangential to the vector field at every point are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14184931/assets/dd47775ffb4cba4cc01dde0bf404dca12bdeecc24e2f58639c04f1feda8293ee.png)",
